   "license": "No explicit open data-reuse license is stated. APS copyright applies to the article; this factual numerical transcription is retained for scientific validation and is not asserted to be openly licensed.",
   "notes": "Table I groups Cu/W/Al in the first two runs and Au/Pt/Ta in the last three runs. Blank metal cells are omitted rather than imputed. P_R is the classical Mao et al. (1986) reduction (A=1904 GPa, B=7.665); P'_R is the Dewaele et al. revision (A=1904 GPa, B=9.5). The paper states a common 0.01 angstrom^3/atom volume uncertainty and a pressure uncertainty increasing from 0.05 GPa at 1 GPa to 2 GPa at 150 GPa, but prints neither row-wise pressure errors nor raw R1 wavelengths.",
   "source_url": "https://harvest.aps.org/v2/journals/articles/10.1103/PhysRevB.70.094112/fulltext"
